      "tables": [],
      "text": "A cooling-off period may be requested at any time after a statement of grounds and particulars has been filed but before the Registrar has made a decision on the opposition or dismissed the opposition (regs 5.16(1), 9.19(1), 17A.34L(1), 17A.48U(1)). Both parties must sign the request for a cooling-off period. There is no fee for requesting a cooling-off period. A cooling-off period must be allowed if the Registrar is satisfied that both parties to the opposition agree to the cooling-off period (regs 5.16(2), 9.19(2), 17A.34L(2), 17A.48U(2))."
    },
    {
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "text": "Only one cooling-off period is allowed in an opposition proceeding (regs 5.16(4), 9.19(4), 17A.34L(4), 17A.48U(4))."
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "text": "The cooling-off period is initially granted for six months (regs 5.16(2), 9.19(2), 17A.34L(2), 17A.48U(2)). The Registrar must extend the cooling-off period for a further 6 months if:"
        },
        {
          "depth": 1,
          "kind": "list_item",
          "text": "a request to extend the cooling-off period is made before the end of the initial six months; and"
        },
        {
          "depth": 1,
          "kind": "list_item",
          "text": "the Registrar is satisfied that both parties agree to the extension (regs 5.16(3), 9.19(3), 17A.34L(3), 17A.48U(3))."
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "text": "A cooling-off period is for a maximum of 12 months. The Registrar cannot further extend a cooling-off period."
        }
      ],
